TimelyNG — a calendar watchface for Pebble

TimelyNG is a watchface for Pebble watches. It shows the current date and
time in the top half (optionally with weather conditions and temperature) and a
small 3-week calendar (previous, current and next week) in the bottom half. The
status bar shows connection, charging and battery level. Text and date formats
are fully localizable through the configuration screen, with options such as
per-hour and link-lost/regained vibration.

This is a modernized fork of the original "Timely" watchface, updated to build
with the current Core Devices Pebble SDK and to run on the new hardware:

  - Pebble Time 2 (emery, color, 200x228)
  - Pebble 2 Duo / Core 2 Duo (flint, black & white, 144x168)
  - and the classic Pebble platforms (aplite, basalt, diorite)

Color is used where the hardware supports it (e.g. the current day is accented
in the calendar) with graceful fallback to black & white on monochrome watches.
Round platforms (chalk / gabbro) are not targeted yet — the layout is
rectangle-centric.

Building (NixOS / Nix, official Pebble CLI flow)

  nix develop                      # pebble CLI + ARM toolchain + emulator
  pebble sdk install latest        # first time only
  pebble build                     # -> build/PebbleTimely.pbw
  pebble install --emulator emery  # color emulator (or basalt / flint / ...)
  pebble login && pebble install --cloudpebble   # to a paired watch

Configuration

The settings screen is fully offline: no server, no CDN, no external host. On
showConfiguration the watch's PebbleKit JS builds the page from src/js/config.js
(the field spec) via src/js/configpage.js and hands it to the phone as a
data:text/html URI; the page returns the chosen values via pebblejs://close#.
Edit src/js/config.js to change the options.

To try it on an emulator: "just config" (guided platform picker via gum) or
"make config EMU=emery" builds, installs, and opens the page (rendered from a
local file so the emulator can round-trip it) so you can pick a theme and see
the watchface update. "just menu" is a guided front-end to all the test tasks.

Tests (pure date/timezone logic, host-compiled, no Pebble SDK)

  nix flake check                  # reproducible
  nix develop .#test -c just test  # or: make test

License

TimelyNG is free software under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or
(at your option) any later version. See LICENSE.

This is a modified version of the original work; significant changes from the
upstream "Timely" include modernization for the current Pebble SDK, support for
the new Core Devices watches (emery / flint), a color theme with monochrome
fallback, and a host-side unit-test suite.

